{"text": "Monica Kelly Chinn\n\nMeticulous PROFESSIONAL STAFFER who values accurate efficiency, thrives in fast-paced settings, and continuously\nendeavors to further build upon institutional and practical knowledge of legislative processes. A quick learner and\nenthusiastic worker who, with myriad experiences in management and workflow design, possesses the ability to think\ncritically, analyze thoughtfully, and work productively both collaboratively and independently. Utilizes research skills to\ndeliver data-driven solutions; believes in good writing and better editing.\n\nexperience:\n\nCOMMITTEE ON RULES, U.S. HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES WASHINGTON, DC JAN 2011-PRESENT\nProfessional Staff (promotions in 2011, 2012, and 2015)\n\u00a2 Coordinates rule resolution production\n\u2014 Operates as a liaison to other committees, Minority staff, and leadership offices on wide portfolio of issues to\nmeet legislative deadlines, prepare for hearings and markups, and produce debate-governing resolutions.\n\u2014 Advises Members and staff on procedural matters relating to floor debate and amendment submission.\n\u2014 Produces resolution and report documents using XMetaL interface for filing on the House floor.\n\ne Responsible for Committee compliance with both internal and House rules\n\u2014 Manages all data collection for publication production of Committee\u2019s Rules, Journal, and Survey of Activities;\ncompiles House Committees\u2019 rules; acts GPO\u2019s Committee point of contact.\n\u2014 Officially notices all Committee activity, balancing timeframe directives with text availability.\n\u2014 Responsible for streamlining paper and electronic amendment intake practices, enabling clerk team to process\nlarge volumes of amendments with heightened accuracy.\n\ne Invested in transparency initiatives, emphasizing online document availability\n\u2014 docs.house.gov: Centralized public online repository for House documents; contributing consultant and Rules\nCommittee administrator since module conception, which hosts all official text for House floor legislation.\nManages timely disclosure of Rules documents for the partnering Committee Repository component.\n\u2014 rules.house.gov: Webmaster managing multiple users to ensure real-time information rollout; overhauled website\nto become a better resource for House users and the public; won CMF\u2019s 113th Congress Gold Mouse Award for\nexemplifying the best of online communications in Congress.\n\nBRAWNER COMPANY WASHINGTON, DC SEPT 2009-OCT 2010\nAssistant Property Manager\n\u2014 Administered diverse property portfolio with commercial, residential, and special use sites; vertical responsibilities\nranged from lease writing and management to fostering tenant and contractor relations to corporate-level accounting.\n\u2014 Spearheaded streamlining of 117,000 sq. ft. commercial building\u2019s operating costs.\n\u2014 Implemented marketing strategy for boutique apartments, including simultaneous website and mobile campaigns.\n\nATLANTIC MEDIA CORPORATION\nArt Department Fellow, Government Executive WASHINGTON, DC JUNE-SEPT 2009\n\n\u2014 Collaborated directly with Art Director and staff writers to heighten editorial content with aesthetics.\n\u2014 Conducted photo research, graphic design, and page layout for converged newsroom of niche magazine.\n\neducation:\n\nWashington and Lee University\nLexington, Virginia 2009\nBachelor of Arts, Journalism and Mass Communications; concentration in Art History\n\ntechnical skills:\n\nComputer: XMetaL Author; Microsoft Office Suite; Adobe Acrobat, InDesign, and Photoshop; Mac and PC literate\nLanguage: French, Intermediate Italian\n\npersonal:\nVolunteer, N Street Village and Folger Shakespeare Library; Junior League of Washington; W&L Track team;\n\ngraphic artist; (5)(l)",
